# File Uploads: Multipart/Form-Data
# Send files and form fields with multipart encoding

@baseUrl = https://api.example.com
@boundary = ----WebKitFormBoundary

###

### Simple file upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}

----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="document.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./document.pdf
----WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### Multiple files
POST {{baseUrl}}/batch-upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}

----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="file1.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./file1.txt
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="file2.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./file2.txt
----WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### File with additional form fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload-with-metadata
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary={{boundary}}

----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

John Doe
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="email"

john@example.com
----WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="resume.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./resume.pdf
----WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### Image upload with description
POST {{baseUrl}}/images/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary123

------Boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

My Photo
------Boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

A beautiful landscape photo
------Boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

nature, sunset, landscape
------Boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./photo.jpg
------Boundary123--

###

### File from relative path
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitBoundary

----WebKitBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="document"; filename="README.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ../README.md
----WebKitBoundary--

###

### CSV file upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/import/csv
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitBoundary

----WebKitBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

users
----WebKitBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="users.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./users.csv
----WebKitBoundary--

###

### File upload with OAuth2
# Combine file upload with OAuth2 authentication

# @oauth2-grant = client_credentials
# @oauth2-token-url = https://auth.example.com/oauth/token
# @oauth2-client-id = {{CLIENT_ID}}
# @oauth2-client-secret = {{CLIENT_SECRET}}
# @oauth2-scope = write
POST {{baseUrl}}/protected/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitBoundary

----WebKitBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="data.json"
Content-Type: application/json

< ./data.json
----WebKitBoundary--

###

### Notes on file uploads:
# 1. Path is relative to the .http file location
# 2. Boundary can be any string (must match in Content-Type header)
# 3. Use same boundary throughout the body
# 4. Each field must start with --boundary
# 5. File content is inserted with: < ./path/to/file
# 6. Last boundary should end with -- (--boundary--)
# 7. Each line must end with CRLF (carriage return + line feed)
